 "sha256": "67c5067751e9f909d2cd875fba5f37350821e293073d4fb7ab57599b007952af",
 "label": "Simulated, not recorded. These responses are the predictions of an uncalibrated computational model (COMSOL Multiphysics\u00ae v. 6.4 ray acoustics; statistical phase synthesised from ray energy) of two states of the theatre: A, an intact Roman hypothesis, and B, the present ruin. This model has not been calibrated against measured impulse responses; it is what our model predicts, not what it sounded like. First-order ambisonic encoding from ray arrival directions at a 1 m-radius collection cylinder; reverberation-time metrics are unreliable outdoors; no absolute level or speech-intelligibility claim.",
 "statistical_label": "STATISTICAL / PERCEPTUAL (ADR 0011 D5). The energies, arrival times and ISO 3382-1 partitions are the echogram's; the PHASE IS SYNTHESISED. Each reflection is a random-phase noise burst carrying the right energy in the right 1 ms bin - there is no coherent wavefront, no comb filtering and no interference with the direct sound. ISO numbers are computed from the echogram and are never back-derived from this waveform.",
 "foa_label": "FOA statistical render: the direct pulse is encoded at the EXACT seat-to-source direction; every reflected ray crossing of the seat's collection cylinder is an independent random-phase band burst carrying that crossing's energy in its 1 ms entry bin, encoded SN3D at its arrival direction. Directions are statistical samples of the arriving field (sparse where few rays crossed - see n_crossings per band), so this is a spatialised statistical IR, not a measured B-format RIR. Per-band W energies, the direct/reflected split and the ISO window partitions close on the echogram exactly as the accepted mono kernel does; per window X, Y and Z share ONE closure gain, so every burst keeps its encoded direction and E_X+E_Y+E_Z = E_W; the noise realisation differs from the mono kernel's.",
